cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use texclaims in published work, please cite it."
title: "texclaims: deterministic auditing of manuscript numbers against experiment artifacts"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that reconciles the numbers written in a LaTeX or
  Markdown manuscript against the fields of the experiment artifacts that
  produced them, through a declarative YAML ledger. It verifies claimed
  numbers at display precision, audits the negative space for numbers no
  claim accounts for, and emits provenance-annotated LaTeX macros so new
  prose need not transcribe results by hand.
type: software
authors:
